---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="End-to-end Lifecycle Automation">
  <h1>End-to-end lifecycle automation</h1>
  <p>
    The intended lifecycle can include issue delegation, code review, security checks, and
    deployment. This rehearsal does not claim that the entire loop has been demonstrated:
  </p>
  <pre>Issue → cloud agent: unverified
Automatic Copilot Code Review: demonstrated independently
Agent Merge: unverified; manual approved merge for this rehearsal
GitHub Actions: tests → audit → build → deploy on main push only</pre>
  <p>
    Local passing checks are not evidence of a successful remote workflow or deployment.
    Verify each step and its actor from actual results before presenting it as completed.
    PR and manual-dispatch runs do not publish this site.
  </p>
  <p>
    That's the goal of "shipping with AI": useful assistance backed by review, repeatable checks,
    and explicit release approval, rather than assuming that automation takes responsibility.
  </p>
</Layout>
